# Build-context filter for the root Dockerfile (M4-W1 provider image).
# Keeps .git, docs, and non-Go tooling out of the `COPY . .` layer so the
# image build doesn't needlessly pull in or cache-bust on unrelated changes.

.git
.github
.claude
docs
runner-images
scripts
*.md
*.local.md
dist/
bin/
coverage.*
*.test
*.out
.DS_Store

# --- Credential deny patterns ---------------------------------------------
#
# The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` copies the WORKING TREE, not what git tracks.
# An operator building this image from their own checkout may have untracked
# local secrets sitting beside the module — a .env, a private key, a client
# certificate, a kubeconfig — and every one of them would otherwise land in
# the builder stage's layer and in the local BuildKit cache (which
# `docker buildx build --cache-to` exports wholesale). The final distroless
# stage copies only the compiled binary, so nothing reaches the published
# image, but the builder layer and the build cache are real exposure.
#
# These are a fail-safe, not a licence to keep secrets in the repo directory.
#
# NOTE ON MATCHING: .dockerignore patterns are matched against the path
# relative to the context root and are NOT recursive unless the pattern says
# so — `*.pem` excludes `./key.pem` but not `./certs/key.pem`. Hence the
# explicit `**/` variants below for extensions that can only ever be
# credential material. Patterns that could plausibly collide with Go source
# (`credentials*`, `secrets*` — cf. the tracked internal/metadata/
# credentials.go) are deliberately left ROOT-ONLY. Do not blindly add `**/`
# to those; it would exclude source files and break the build.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.crt
**/*.crt
*.cer
**/*.cer
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
*.jks
**/*.jks
*.keystore
**/*.keystore
*.kdbx
*.gpg
*.asc
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
**/id_ed25519*
*.ppk
known_hosts
.ssh/
.netrc
**/.netrc
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.pypirc
**/.pypirc
.aws/
**/.aws/
.gcloud/
**/.gcloud/
.kube/
**/.kube/
.docker/
**/.docker/
secrets*
credentials*
service-account*.json
**/*service-account*.json
*.tfvars
*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
